WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.790
- [Mark] Craig?

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.050
- Yes.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.244
- [Mark] Where you from, originally?

00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:16.077
- Cerritos.

00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:18.152
- [Mark] Cerritos, and how
long you been here on Skid Row?

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:19.423
- [Craig] Since 2000.

00:00:19.423 --> 00:00:22.253
- [Mark] Since 2000. What happened to you,

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.743
that you ended up down here?

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.913
- [Craig] Just too lazy,
didn't want to work.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.290
- [Mark] You just didn't
feel like working?

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:30.123
- [Craig] Yeah.

00:00:30.123 --> 00:00:32.180
- [Mark] So, living down here,
there's no responsibility.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.590
- Yes.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:34.446
- [Mark] No hassles?

00:00:34.446 --> 00:00:35.279
- No hassles.

00:00:35.279 --> 00:00:36.112
- [Mark] Very simple?

00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:37.190
- Very simple.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:38.720
- [Mark] You go to the
mission to get your dinner?

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.553
- Yes I do.

00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:40.386
- [Mark] And breakfast, probably?

00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:41.219
- Yes.

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:42.760
- [Mark] How about lunch?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.110
- You know, I eat on the, on the road.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.800
- [Mark] Yeah. Do you panhandle?

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.210
- Yes.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.330
- [Mark] And what about drugs?

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:50.693
Do you do any of the
drugs that are down here?

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:52.346
- Weed and drink beer.

00:00:52.346 --> 00:00:54.070
- [Mark] That's it?
That's nothing compared to

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.240
what else goes on around here.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.073
- Yeah.

00:00:58.928 --> 00:01:01.583
- [Mark] And then, now,
where do you sleep?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.610
- Anywhere on the streets.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.443
- [Mark] Wherever you can?

00:01:04.443 --> 00:01:05.276
- Yeah.

00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:11.633
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:01:11.633 --> 00:01:12.466
- 49.

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:13.990
- [Mark] 49.

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.793
And tell me about your childhood.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.410
- I just grew up in a good
house, in a household.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:23.370
My parents, they worked.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.203
- [Mark] No abuse?

00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:27.230
- No abuse, no drugs.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.063
- [Mark] No nothing?

00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:28.896
- Just work.

00:01:28.896 --> 00:01:29.729
- [Mark] You just don't feel like

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:31.060
taking on the responsibility?

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.230
- Yeah, work.

00:01:32.230 --> 00:01:34.807
- [Mark] Of life and
work, and having a job and

00:01:34.807 --> 00:01:37.073
paying bills and all that?

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.123
Do you think you're happy?

00:01:39.123 --> 00:01:40.270
Do you feel like you're happy this way?

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.103
- Yes, I do.

00:01:41.103 --> 00:01:42.910
- [Mark] Yeah. You seem pretty content.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.633
And where would you like to
see yourself in five years?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.220
- I couldn't tell you.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.170
Just have my life-

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.320
Not necessarily in an
apartment or anything.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.153
Just...

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:01.423
doing right.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.093
- [Mark] And did you feel like you're

00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:04.130
not doing right, right now?

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.020
- Yeah.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:05.940
- [Mark] What's what's going on now?

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.273
- Oh, just like my clothes are dirty.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.820
No shower.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:12.880
Just doing right.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.730
- [Mark] Yeah, but that's easy to fix.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:14.733
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.358
- [Mark] Excellent, do
you have any other family?

00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:19.316
Are your parents still around?

00:02:19.316 --> 00:02:20.224
- No, no.

00:02:20.224 --> 00:02:21.057
- [Mark] So it's just you?

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:21.890
- Yeah.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:22.723
- [Mark] Were you an only child?

00:02:22.723 --> 00:02:23.556
- Yes.

00:02:23.556 --> 00:02:25.525
- [Mark] Okay.

00:02:25.525 --> 00:02:29.330
And, do you have any girlfriends,
or plan on, have no kids?

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:30.172
- No, no.

00:02:30.172 --> 00:02:31.415
- [Mark] Okay, do you ever
have, or anything like that?

00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:32.248
- No.

00:02:32.248 --> 00:02:33.660
- [Mark] You've never had
relationships? Never had any?

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.243
- I've had one relationship with Laurie,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.100
and it was a good one

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.483
and it lasted for like couple years.

00:02:43.804 --> 00:02:45.520
And we went by our separate way.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.340
I still talk to her, she's good.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.403
She's a nice person.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.730
She's just not really my type.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:53.843
She's sort of fat.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.220
Whether or not, we alright.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.506
- [Mark] Do you have any friends?

00:03:01.506 --> 00:03:03.700
- [Craig] No- Yeah, yeah I got friends.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.730
I got a lot of associates,
I call them associates.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.460
- [Mark] People that you
see a lot on the street?

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.500
- [Craig] Yeah, yeah.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:09.770
- [Mark] But they're not
really like tight friends?

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:10.603
- [Craig] No.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.981
- [Mark] And your health
is good? You feel fine?

00:03:14.981 --> 00:03:15.814
- [Craig] Yeah, yeah.

00:03:15.814 --> 00:03:17.740
- [Mark] And you say drinking, weed,

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:20.560
you don't get out of
control with that or you do?

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:21.763
- [Craig] Actually I don't. No.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:25.210
- [Mark] You're just avoiding
all the stress of life.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.239
- [Craig] Yeah.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.489
(laughter)

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:33.090
- [Mark] You picked the right
city to do that in, LA's warm.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:40.140
You've seen some crazy stuff
down here in Skid Row, right?

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.370
- [Craig] Actually, I haven't.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.000
I've heard about it,
but I haven't seen it.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.660
- [Mark] So you tend
to stay away from the-

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.493
- [Craig] Drama?

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.326
- [Mark] The drama.

00:03:48.326 --> 00:03:49.159
- [Craig] Yes.

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:50.240
- [Mark] Yeah, so you're
sleeping somewhere

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.730
closer to downtown or federal buildings...

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.760
- [Craig] Yeah, to missions.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.593
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:03:55.593 --> 00:03:57.010
- I sleep closer to the missions.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.610
- [Mark] Oh, I see. Okay, cool.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:03:59.443
- It's safe.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.460
- [Mark] Well thank you for talking to me.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:05.293
- [Craig] Yeah.

00:04:05.293 --> 00:04:06.411
- [Mark] I appreciate it.

00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:07.244
Be safe out there.

00:04:07.244 --> 00:04:08.077
- [Craig] I will.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.600
- Hey, if I tell you a funny
joke, can I earn another 20?

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.340
If I tell you a funny joke?

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.871
Help me out, I need
another 20, help me out.

00:04:19.871 --> 00:04:21.450
(laughter)

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.320
- [Mark] I'll tell you
what, if you make me laugh,

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.398
I'll give you another 20.

00:04:23.398 --> 00:04:24.231
- Alright.

00:04:24.231 --> 00:04:25.830
- [Mark] No, no stay put.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:27.650
- Can you hear this? Say, "No."

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:28.483
Say "No."

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:30.893
- [Mark] No.

00:04:30.893 --> 00:04:32.244
- Let me turn it up for you.

00:04:32.244 --> 00:04:33.320
(laughter)

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.810
- [Mark] Alright, you're good.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:37.540
- Thank you, I can walk from here.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.160
- [Mark] Really?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:39.993
- Yeah.

